00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:01.910 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  welcome back it's not just new york  because michigan governor gretchen  whitmer is also  facing intense scrutiny for her handling  of covet 19 in nursing homes  and family members are demanding answers  including our next guest  who lost her mother jamie nicholson is  here now to share her story  jamie thank you for joining us i'm so  sorry um to talk to you under these  circumstances but we appreciate you  giving us your time and sharing your  story  thank you jylen let's talk about your  mother nancy  um i know that she was 76 when she  passed away i know that you cared for  her tremendously  at great length for 16 years after she  was diagnosed with alzheimer's  tell me what happened there last year  thank you jillian dad and i worked  so hard and loved mom so much in caring  for her  and on march 11th the  of last year at mom's nursing home  locked us out  dad and i were prohibited from any  physical contact with mom for 11 months  in the final month of her life she was  faced with even more  restrictions moved to a different  facility  and finally died of depression and  loneliness  we watched her over 11 months fade away  and die  through a window and on screens  my heart breaks for you what was the the  best thing about your mother tell me  about her  mom uh had a vibrant personality  even though she was in her different  facilities dependent  fully dependent on care for the last  three years of her life everyone around  her  remarked at her smile her  energy her laughter i would take her  dancing in her wheelchair  and swing it around and play music i'd  clear out all the  the chairs and tables in the cafeteria  and put on the 50s  and she would just light up and and hold  my hand and  and dad would come and hold her hand and  watch  their favorite shows together even when  she was institutionalized  because he loved her so much sounds like  a beautiful woman and you sound like a  beautiful family  i'm going to keep you here with us i'm  going to bring in ted goodman who's a  spokesman for  michigan's republican party you know ted  i know lawmakers are requesting an  investigation of what happened here and  and governor whitmer's handling of this  pandemic  can you tell me a little bit about where  you stand on this and how you're trying  to go about getting answers  sure uh and of course uh our hearts go  out  uh to the family and and all the loved  ones we've lost over the course of this  pandemic  such a heartbreaking story we just heard  and this story is playing out  repeatedly across the state of michigan  and in many parts of this country  so macomb county prosecutor pete lecito  announced yesterday at a press  conference that he is  looking for individuals who may have  lost loved ones inside nursing homes  and assisted care facilities to file a  police report  with macomb county police because the  hipaa laws  do not allow the prosecutor to gain  access the information he needs  to find out the truth about these  nursing home policies  and what happened that may have led to  unnecessary  and avoidable deaths jamie has it been  hard for you to to watch the the fight  that's been going on  in new york and certainly i mean look  all of the attention  is warranted and deserved in new york in  michigan wherever else this could have  happened throughout this country  for families to be able to get answers  but a lot of the focus the last you know  few months has been on new york and just  now  we're talking about michigan do you feel  like you're a step forward now and  trying to get answers  we a dad and i talk about this regularly  jillian and it's hard we you know it's  hard for us to turn on the tv dad hasn't  even looked at the cards that have come  in the mail  with sympathy but let me tell you it  also  strengthens our resolve another thing  about mom was she was a fighter  and that's something that i inherited  from her  and learned from her and and i am ready  i was  talking with senator jim runstad and  he encouraged me to to gather our forces  and mobilize people as much as we could  we  we came up with this group on facebook  like the parents of  athletes who organized 30 000 people and  and got on the steps of the capitol and  had a rally and  and then shortly thereafter uh the  governor  changed her policies and allowed those  uh  individuals and so we want to do that  too we have our facebook  book group called save our seniors  michigan and  we are organizing and we are in this  fight together so that nobody has to go  through  what we did absolutely well we do know  that governor whitmer stands by the  nursing home policy we know that that  she had ended that practice after the  first six months of the pandemic but  still i mean there are a lot of people  just like yourself  who want answers to these questions um  we appreciate you both joining us  that's all the time we have a ted  goodman and jamie nicholson thank you  very much i'm sorry for your loss jamie  we'll be right back

